# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

## Summary
Successfully implemented Vercel Web Analytics for the Flowora static HTML project by adding the analytics script tag to all HTML pages.

## Implementation Details

### Project Type
This is a static HTML website without a build system or package manager. It uses vanilla HTML, CSS, and JavaScript with Tailwind CSS v4 CDN.

### Approach Used
According to the latest Vercel Analytics documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), for static HTML projects, the recommended approach is to include the analytics script via CDN.

### Files Modified
Added the Vercel Analytics script tag to all HTML files in the project:

1. **main-files/index.html** (line 46)
   - Main landing page
   
2. **main-files/404.html** (line 46)
   - 404 error page
   
3. **main-files/blog-detail.html** (line 46)
   - Blog detail page
   
4. **main-files/documentation/index.html** (line 36)
   - Documentation page

### Script Added
```html
<!-- Vercel Web Analytics -->
<script defer src="https://cdn.vercel-insights.com/v1/script.js"></script>
```

### Script Placement
The analytics script was placed just before the closing `</head>` tag in each HTML file, following best practices:
- Uses `defer` attribute to load the script asynchronously without blocking page rendering
- Positioned after other critical resources but before the closing head tag
- Consistent placement across all pages for easy maintenance

## How It Works
- The script loads from Vercel's CDN (https://cdn.vercel-insights.com/v1/script.js)
- It automatically tracks page views when deployed on Vercel
- The `defer` attribute ensures the script doesn't block page rendering
- Analytics data will be available in the Vercel dashboard after deployment

## Next Steps
Once this is deployed to Vercel:
1. Enable Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Analytics section in sidebar)
2. Verify the script is loading by checking the Network tab in browser DevTools
3. Look for requests to analytics endpoints
4. Analytics data will appear in the dashboard after some visitor traffic

## Notes
- No package.json or build process required for this implementation
- This is the official CDN approach recommended by Vercel for static HTML sites
- The script is lightweight and won't impact page performance
- Works automatically when deployed to Vercel's platform
